#      Education -> Employment <- Health -> Earnings - Employement is a collider
#
# Q12. Is this path open or closed if we do NOT condition on Employment? - the path is closed if we do not condition on Employment
#
# Q13. What can happen if we control for Employment? - If we control for Employment we will open a back door path
#
# Q14. Imagine that our dataset contains earnings only for people who are
#      currently employed. Why could this create a problem? - This would create a type of sampling error which would then interefer with the causality
#
# Now ask Dagitty for an adjustment set for the TOTAL effect:
adjustmentSets(dag3)
#      Education -> Employment <- Health -> Earnings - Employement is a collider
#
# Q12. Is this path open or closed if we do NOT condition on Employment? - the path is closed if we do not condition on Employment
#
# Q13. What can happen if we control for Employment? - If we control for Employment we will open a back door path
#
# Q14. Imagine that our dataset contains earnings only for people who are
#      currently employed. Why could this create a problem? - This would create a type of sampling error which would then cause bias in the causal association meaning it will not represent the relationships of the wider population accurately
#
# Now ask Dagitty for an adjustment set for the TOTAL effect:
adjustmentSets(dag3)
